t` is a symlink while taking `os.path.dirname(current)` lexically when `current` is a non-symlink directory so an x-only (`0111`/`0311`) directory on the way is not arm 2, along with their required unit tests (`test_dot_component_does_not_shift_dotdot`, `test_claude_dot_then_dotdot_into_production_denies`, `test_dotdot_after_symlink_follows_the_kernel`, `test_dotdot_through_unreadable_directory_is_lexical`) and mutations (`TI8`, `TI9`, `TI10`, `TI11`).\n  class: build\n  quote: docs/01-plan/features/tdd-gate-fail-opens.impl-plan.md › `\u003e Source: docs/02-design/features/tdd-gate-fail-opens.design.md v1.2 (48d639f7), the contract.`\n  quote: docs/02-design/features/tdd-gate-fail-opens.design.md › `N-1: in the canonicaliser's `..` rule, an existing non-symlink directory takes `os.path.dirname(current)` and does not open it, so an x-only directory on the way is not arm 2 (the symlink branch still opens the referent). The walk skips `.` components (mutation TI10; pins test_dot_component_does_not_shift_dotdot, test_claude_dot_then_dotdot_into_production_denies): a kept `.` let the next `..` strip only itself, so `tests/./../src/prod.py` resolved under tests/ and the Claude gate allowed it, a fail-open already on main before v1.6 (found by fresh-context review).`\n- Task 5 instructs reading `reap_failed` in `judge()` **before** the `# M:K3` line (`kind = \"no-summary\" if error else score(out + \"\\n\" + err, timed_out)  # M:K3`) while keeping the `# M:K3` line byte-identical; if `# M:K3` stays unindented and runs after `reap_failed`, it unconditionally overwrites `kind = \"judge-timeout\"` with `score(..., True)` (`\"timeout\"`), whereas indenting `# M:K3` under `else:` mutates its leading whitespace and breaks existing mutation anchors `K3` and `K3B` in `h-mad/tests/mutation-specs/tdd_judge_scoring.json` (`if reap_failed: kind = \"judge-timeout\"` must instead follow `# M:K3`, as implemented in `h-mad/scripts/h_mad_tdd_judge.py`).\n  class: build\n  quote: docs/01-pl